// B1's race rule, the STATEFUL refusal: two spawned branches performing
// `bump` into ONE `counter` install at the fanout's frame would resume
// `with n = n + 1` on one shared state record from two instances — a
// definite race, refused at lowering (E_ThreadedBranchEffect names Counter
// and the stateful handler). Each branch installing its own counter runs
// (mn-threaded-branch-inner-install); a stateless handler runs
// (mn-threaded-branch-stateless).
// Expected: REFUSE E_ThreadedBranchEffect.
effect Counter { bump() -> Int }
handler counter with n = 5 { bump() => resume(n) with n = n + 1 }
fn main() = match (0 <| ({ _ => bump() }, { _ => bump() })) ~> parallel_compose ~> counter {
  (a, b) => a + b,
}
